  {
   "path": "reflection.example.steps.en",
   "before": "Write down first where the differences between the two groups could come from: besides the process itself, what else could explain the gap in results?\nPick the most dangerous rival explanation and find one piece of evidence that pins it down — a comparison within the same class of customer, the equivalent of Snow's single street.\nCompare only data you are confident in; skip suspect breakdowns, and turn the gap into plain language (one runs at several times the rate of the other) before reaching for a complicated model.\nSet a line for action: how large the gap must be and how well the rival explanations must be pinned down before you switch. Below the line, keep watching — and write down the date to look again.",
   "after": "Write down first where the differences between the two groups could come from: besides the process itself, what else could explain the gap in results?\nPick the most dangerous rival explanation and find one piece of evidence that pins it down — a comparison within the same class of customer, the equivalent of Snow's comparison within the same intermixed streets.\nCompare only data you are confident in; skip suspect breakdowns, and turn the gap into plain language (one runs at several times the rate of the other) before reaching for a complicated model.\nSet a line for action: how large the gap must be and how well the rival explanations must be pinned down before you switch. Below the line, keep watching — and write down the date to look again.",
